## Proposed replacement for subject-only merging

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is an accepted historical record;
leave it unchanged. The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) still applies its rule, reviewed
in June 2024. Its render-time stale warning is a reason to check the evidence. The concrete
counterexamples below are why the rule needs replacement, regardless of its age.
This record proposes that replacement; desk acceptance and updating the triage page remain pending.

<DedupeExplorer />

- Different subjects can describe the same cause: app and email from `kettle.books`.
- The same subject can hide different causes: form and app from `alder.physio`.
- The same subject and channel can hide different causes: `copper.studio` and `morrow.tax` forms.
- Unknown tenants are unplaced; a matching subject does not justify merging them.

Deduplicate export rows by report ID first. Then read each body and look up the tenant's
locale, booking-form version, and entry channel. Use the classifier as evidence, check for
contradicting symptoms, and merge only when the underlying problem matches. Keep uncertain
reports for investigation rather than forcing them into a familiar cause.

Engineering should track each confirmed cause separately, retain each report ID and its
assignment, and verify each fix against representative inputs. Re-read and render this page
when new exports arrive: these components recompute their results from the files at build time.

